  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the rule now exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view findings** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, 14,074 docs)\n- Key fields: `@timestamp`/`timestamp`, `response` (numeric status code), `bytes`, `clientip`, `request`/`url`, `geo.*`, `machine.*`, `agent`.\n- Status codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). All 5xx responses are 503.\n- Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, which is partly in the future relative to today (2026-10-12).\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-e4af1d89 Web logs overview`** (id `ee590d77-412d-4be3-8091-17cf6df4a80f`)\n- A markdown header.\n- Metric panels for total requests, 5xx server errors (`response >= 500`), and unique client IPs.\n- XY panels for requests over time and 5xx errors over time, both using date histograms.\n\n**Rule: `EFF-e4af1d89 5xx spike`** (id `47f50928-afda-426a-b223-98a832d1fec5`)\n- Type `.es-query`, enabled, runs every 1m.\n- Counts docs with `response` between 500 and 599 over a 5-minute window on `timestamp`.\n- Fires when the count is `> 10`.\n- Its first run returned status `ok`.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- **Consumer `stackAlerts`**, the usual owner for ES query rules.\n- **No actions or connectors.** The rule will record alerts but won't send notifications.\n- **Action group size of 10**, which is how many matching docs get passed to actions. It has no effect while there are no actions.\n\nThe rule only fires if 5xx docs land in the last 5 minutes of wall-clock time. The sample data is dated in the future, so it may never fire here. I did not force a firing.\n\nTwo housekeeping notes: a hung command left one empty stray file, `/tmp/eff-dssscyse/q1.json`, which I removed. I also created the scratch request files under the session scratchpad, not in the work directory.",
